3.2 \(F(a,b;c;z)\)=\(\frac{\Gamma(e)}{2\pi i\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}\int_{-t_{\infty}}^{t_{\infty}}\frac{ \Gamma(a+s)\Gamma(b+s)\Gamma(-s)}{\Gamma(e+s)}\left(-z\right)^{*}\!ds\)

Here \(-\pi\!\!<\!\!\arg(-z)\!\!<\!\!\pi\) and the path of integration is chosen such that the poles of \(\Gamma(a\!+\!s)\) and \(\Gamma(b\!+\!s)\) i.e. the points \(s\!=\!-a\!-n\) and \(s\!=\!-b\!-\!m\!\left(n,\ m\!=\!0,\ 1,\ 2,\ \ldots\ \right)\) respectively, are at its left side and the poles of \(\mathrm{esc}\!\left(\pi s\right)\) or \(\Gamma(-s)\) i.e. \(s\!=\!0,1,2\), are at its right side. The cases in which \(-a,\,-b\) or \(-c\) are non-negative integers or \(a\!-\!b\) equal to an integer are excluded.

### Linear Transformation Formulas

From 15.3.1 and 15.3.2 a number of transformation formulas for \(F(a,b;c;z)\) can be derived.

